WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.140
Sometimes when Donald Trump does something,
we call it humiliating, but it's only humiliating

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.479
if you have a certain sensibility.

00:00:06.479 --> 00:00:09.550
It's only humiliating if you have a certain
world view.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:15.640
Donald Trump last night gave an interview
to Fox News's Sean Hannity that was so cringeworthy,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:21.340
so disgusting, that the humiliation has spread
much farther than you can imagine.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:27.810
Sean Hannity actually brought up the story
of Donald Trump allegedly calling dead soldiers

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.119
who died in combat suckers and the losers.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:36.289
And Donald Trump focused in on the idea that
it's not true, that he didn't want to be out

00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:41.210
in the rain in France, and that that's part
of why Donald Trump didn't go, that Donald

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:46.359
Trump says, I've been out in the rain many
times and my hair gets wet and it's no big

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:47.420
deal.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:53.000
This is the level of discussion that is happening
with the president of the United States on

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.839
one of the top rated cable news shows.

00:00:54.839 --> 00:00:58.480
We have a raging pandemic with nearly 200000
deaths.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.209
We have all sorts of economic problems.

00:01:00.209 --> 00:01:02.639
We are on the precipice of a major election.

00:01:02.639 --> 00:01:06.560
And Donald Trump is on cable news saying it's
okay if my hair gets wet.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.710
I made a speech in the rain.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.170
No umbrellas, no anything.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.940
You know, they said just this information.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.280
I didn't want to get my hair wet.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.220
I've had my hair wet plenty of times.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.020
I made plenty of speeches in the rain.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.400
And if I wasn't, if I didn't, you wouldn't
be president right now.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.400
That I can tell you.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.070
So it's disinformation.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:27.530
They made up a story about two disgusting
words that they say.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:28.870
I said and I didn't.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.190
And I have many witnesses.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.310
We have twenty one witnesses.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.960
They only have sources.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:39.880
Of course, Trump doesn't seem to realize that
a witness to something saying you didn't say

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:45.409
it is a weird thing if someone comes forward
and says, I didn't hear Trump say it.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:46.409
That's not proof.

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:47.409
It wasn't said.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:49.000
All it means is you didn't hear it.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.250
And it's it's very difficult, of course, to
prove a negative.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.250
That's by it.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.250
By its very nature.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.250
Hard to do.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.250
Donald Trump doesn't seem to get that.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.580
And he insists, listen, Zach said some guy
named Zach Zach said, I didn't say it.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.070
Well, that just means he didn't hear you say
it.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:09.640
Earlier this week, I reported to you that
Donald Trump's campaign is tight on cash.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.330
They have had to slow down ad spending in
some key states.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.319
The fundraising is a problem.

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:20.180
And Sean Hannity, this is I mean, this is
how you turn manure into gold or at least

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.409
attempt to.

00:02:21.409 --> 00:02:25.540
Sean Hannity hilariously asked, Donald Trump
is not buying ads.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.959
A strategy like is not having money, maybe
a strategy, even check this out.

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:31.760
Say that is not the case.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.920
Yeah, little shy of 300 million dollars.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:40.890
But I was told by a friend in Florida that
that Joe Biden has three to one ads running

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.329
against Jaws.

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:47.099
Is this a strategy you're waiting or is this
something that you didn't want?

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.450
Maybe you're just ramping up after Labor Day.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:55.329
So four years ago, I wanted in the last month
and we have about three times more cash now

00:02:55.329 --> 00:02:56.329
than we had then.

00:02:56.329 --> 00:02:58.560
And that's without me putting up any of I
needed extra.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.560
I'll put it up myself.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.489
I just said that two days ago.

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:06.810
I said if there's any necessary extra cash,
but we have a lot of money coming in and small

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:07.810
donors.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.599
I haven't been heavy on big donors because
I don't want to call them.

00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:14.150
You know, when you call big donors, you you
sort of put yourself in a very compromising

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.209
position.

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:21.290
Trump knows how compromising it is to get
money from donors because he spent the last

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.269
four years doing favors to his donors.

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:30.510
And it's very interesting to hear Donald Trump
say we won it in the last month in 2016.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.150
This is not a guarantee of anything.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.329
Of course, Joe Biden's lead today, today is
seven point.

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:43.739
Five nationally, Hillary's lead on this day
in 2016 was two point seven.

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:49.409
So today, Joe Biden's lead is nearly three
times as large as Hillary's was at this time

00:03:49.409 --> 00:03:50.870
in 2016.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.540
It doesn't mean Trump is going to lose.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:04:00.519
But Trump saying this year is just like 2016
is assuming a lot in 2016.

00:04:00.519 --> 00:04:03.379
Donald Trump was not already the president
in 2016.

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:08.370
Donald Trump was much closer to his opponent
than where he is today.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.829
That those are just factual differences.

00:04:10.829 --> 00:04:16.871
Then Donald Trump goes on to say that right
now the United States has a record number

00:04:16.871 --> 00:04:18.140
of jobs.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.610
What that means is a question.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:24.160
We don't know what they're doing, frankly,
but they should all be open.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.790
And our country is doing very well.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.770
We have record numbers of jobs.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:30.890
You saw the numbers just came out for the
four months.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:34.190
It's the largest number ever by far.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.310
Not even close.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.950
So we do not have a record number of jobs
right now.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.810
Donald Trump has no idea what he's talking
about.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:45.190
Remember that the big picture numbers are
we lost close to 50 million jobs during the

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.980
pandemic.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:48.850
Many of those have come back.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.040
OK, but we are still way down.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:56.320
The idea that we have more jobs than ever
is something that you have a tough time convincing

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:01.450
a 12 year old of even a smart nine year old
probably wouldn't fall for it.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:04.450
But Donald Trump throws out this generality.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.950
We have the record number of jobs.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.220
It's very much untrue.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:10.330
You're not going to hear any fact checking
of it from Sean Hannity.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:14.950
And then also continuing to spread what at
this point is just embarrassing disinformation.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:19.210
Donald Trump claiming that if you look at
our coronavirus numbers, that they're actually

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.210
amazing.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.490
It's just incredible how well we've done.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:24.900
There's two million, two and a half million,
maybe even more than that, if we did it a

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.390
different way and we've done a really good
job.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:32.540
But if you look at our numbers, our fatality
numbers compared to other countries we're

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.530
in, we're in.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.720
Really I mean, it's amazing what we've done.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.380
We've been able to do something that a country,
especially with the kind of size we're dealing

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.550
with, we've done an incredible job.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:48.670
The truth there, of course, is our numbers
are really, really bad.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:54.770
Now, if you don't adjust for our population,
the U.S. has by far the most coronavirus deaths.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:58.080
But we also have a lot of people we really
need to be looking at per capita numbers on

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.950
a per capita basis.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:03.640
The United States is 11th highest in the world.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:07.820
Out of more than 200 countries and territories
in terms of deaths per capita.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:13.610
Now, if you take out some of these tiny countries
and territories, which can skew the numbers

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:21.500
like San Marino and Andorra, the United States
has the ninth highest deaths per capita from

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.560
Corona virus in the world.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.560
It's not the lowest.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.900
It's not in the bottom half.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.900
It is the ninth highest in the world.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:35.880
Question to you, when Trump says this stuff,
when Trump says we have more jobs than ever.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.510
When Trump says we have the best corona virus
numbers in the world.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:41.920
Do people believe it?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.440
Are there people who hear Trump say it and
think Trump's right?

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:46.880
We've done such a great job.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.940
We're so much better off than every other
country.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:54.470
Or is it just something he has to say, even
if no one is going to believe it?

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.460
I actually don't know the answer.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.670
I know there are people who do think we're
doing well on the virus, but I don't know

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.640
that they think it because Donald Trump is
the one saying it.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.110
Let me know your thoughts.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.650
And bigger picture.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.490
Does an interview like this do trump any favors?

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:13.760
Is this a net gain for Trump in some way to
be interviewed by Sean Hannity, even if he

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:17.090
makes no sense in ways that I can't exactly
understand?

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:20.470
Does this do damage or does it really not
make a difference whatsoever?

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:27.880
If you look at the sort of framework of Allan
Lichtman, who predicts elections using a qualitative

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:32.560
rather than quantitative system, he would
argue, I think, that this doesn't matter,

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.830
that really what impacts the election are
big issues.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.670
What is the status of the economy?

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:41.280
Is there a major calamity, et cetera?

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.740
There are others who may have a different
perspective.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:49.420
Let me know in general, do interviews like
this have any impact on the election result?

00:07:49.420 --> 00:09:11.280
We would expect.

